Usage: hops fg [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Feature group commands.

Options:
  --json                  Output as JSON (machine-readable; for LLMs and
                          scripts).
  --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-verify
                          skips verification for self-signed / IP-SAN-
                          mismatched certs.
  -h, --help              Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  add-keyword      Attach a keyword (tag) to a feature group.
  append-features  Append new columns to an existing feature group, in...
  create           Register a new feature group in the feature store.
  create-external  Register an external feature group backed by a storage...
  delete           Delete a feature group and all its data.
  derive           Create a new feature group derived from joining...
  features         List the schema of a feature group (name, type,...
  info             Print metadata for a single feature group.
  insert           Insert rows into a feature group from a file, stdin,...
  keywords         Show all tags attached to a feature group (aka keywords).
  lineage          Show upstream and downstream lineage for a feature group.
  list             List feature groups across every feature store the...
  preview          Show the first ``n`` rows of a feature group.
  remove-keyword   Remove a keyword (tag) from a feature group.
  search           Run a KNN similarity search against a feature group's...
  stats            Show or recompute statistics for a feature group.
===SQL===
Usage: hops sql [OPTIONS] [SQL]

  Run an ad-hoc SQL query.

  Provide the SQL as a positional argument, or use ``-f`` to read from a file,
  or ``-i`` to read from stdin (useful in shell pipelines).

  Args:     ctx: Click context.     sql: SQL string passed positionally.
  sql_file: Path to a file containing SQL.     from_stdin: Read SQL from
  standard input.     catalog: Trino catalog override.     schema: Trino
  schema override.     limit: Soft cap on rows printed.

Options:
  -f, --file FILE         Read SQL from a file.
  -i, --stdin             Read SQL from standard input.
  --catalog TEXT          Trino catalog (default: iceberg).
  --schema TEXT           Trino schema (default: project name lowercased).
  --limit INTEGER         Soft cap on rows printed; 0 means unlimited.
                          [default: 10000]
  --json                  Output as JSON (machine-readable; for LLMs and
                          scripts).
  --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-verify
                          skips verification for self-signed / IP-SAN-
                          mismatched certs.
  -h, --help              Show this message and exit.
